Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Behaviours:
- Make sidebar New thread and chat.new respect combined machine/include/exclude filters, ignoring search text. Start directly for one reachable project member, offer a restricted picker for several, and open the full upstream list with an unreachable note when no target is reachable.
- With several selected machines, rank each project's selected members online first, then by latest existing thread update/creation activity; ties or absent activity use primary-first catalog order. Keep separate clone choices on the chosen machine. Preserve singleton behavior and treat empty, unknown, all-known and fewer-than-two-machine scopes as unfiltered.
- Without a filter, preserve upstream current-project behavior with one open project group; default and grouped multi-project sidebars show the full list. Preserve Shift-click/current-project shortcuts, Shift-over-Alt precedence and the zero-project disabled button.
- Restricted pickers show explicit project/machine members including separate clones, with primary machine first, then project activity, and offline members last/disabled. A singleton scoped offline member can offer reachable siblings; several-machine targeting chooses an online in-scope sibling before an offline member, so the unreachable note appears only when no filtered project is reachable. Reuse quiet client data without a visit map, traffic or storage.
- Full and unreachable pickers preserve upstream grouped rows, contextual environment choice, load balancing, offline handling and No project's position. Alt-click and widening use that list. Palette-root New thread in always remains full, stably promoting reachable filter matches and recomputing from live metadata/connectivity/filter inputs while open.
- Carry contextual headings and frozen restricted members through the palette. Empty-query Backspace, Back and the persistent All projects row widen; Escape cancels. Restricted searches cannot fall through to root commands or filesystem browsing. Already-open palettes keep upstream shortcut behavior: run a matching displayed item or do nothing.
- Exact active keybindings win over the Alt-plus-chat.new fallback, which applies only to otherwise unbound chords; preserve mod+alt+n for No project, physical/remapped keys and conditional bindings.
- Share exact-member creation for direct and restricted picks. Reuse empty drafts only for the exact project and environment, including unmapped/concurrent drafts; pin explicit members against load balancing while preserving model/workspace defaults and history. Scratch members use startScratchThread like No project.
- Subscribe to project activity only for two or more explicitly scoped machines. Keep tooltips reactive to filter, metadata, connectivity and the same activity used by click-time targeting, naming the exact project and machine for direct creation. Show Shift hints only when plain click differs and Alt hints only when plain click does not already open all projects.
- Document filtered/unfiltered starts, selected-machine activity choice, widening, modifiers, No project, draft reuse and history. Folder pens, agent/MCP creation, providers and native mobile retain their upstream behavior; web, Electron renderer and mobile browser share the behavior.
- Reuse the shared project-scope environment filter in production targeting. Read only the active project-filter mode for both click-time and reactive new-thread targeting, so the Hide list retained by Cmd/Ctrl Show only never excludes the chosen project. Keep selector empty-list identities stable for Zustand shallow snapshots.

Integration details:
- Preserve current upstream one-open-project context policy and the picker in both default and grouped multi-project sidebars; keep archived-only/no-current fallback to the full palette. Use all/open group counts for tooltip and click agreement.
- Exclude archived groups and archived exact members from filtered targets; treat archived-on-the-selected-machine keys as inactive in singleton machine scope, matching the sidebar while preserving global metadata for multiple selected machines. Retain pinned ordering and ignore archived-member activity. Recheck member existence/archive status before exact creation.
- Preserve full-picker frozen pin ordering, No-project position, Add-project fallback, listed/visible-thread filtering and environment-keyed group lookup. Forward event.target through Alt fallback so editable-focus conditions remain correct. Update upstream browser/shortcut fixtures for the shared action and explicit full-target payload.

Port to 965ddc1d6c:
- Upstream #33131 removed the legacy sidebar setting. Sidebar New thread, chat.new and startNewThreadInSidebarFilter no longer read legacySidebarEnabled: without a filter the current project opens only with exactly one open project group. The legacy-sidebar case is gone from useHandleNewThread.test.ts and the legacy sentence from docs/user/thread-sidebar.md.
- Upstream #33109 labels the current project in New thread in. buildNewThreadInProjectItems takes both upstream's currentProjectKey and this commit's isOnline, so ProjectLocationDescription can show Current and (Offline); restricted pickers pass currentProjectKey null, and the full list keeps upstream's label and order.

